From b3f97c9fb060b7b399ca41c39e280d1d365ee428 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grafici patch export <patch-export@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:34:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Define interpolation endpoints and validate bounded knot
 pairs

M>=2 output samples now cover i/(M-1), including both endpoints. A single
output returns the first knot; zero outputs or fewer than two input points
produce an empty source. Uncovered portions of a declared x range return
invalid samples rather than extrapolating or reading bin+1 out of bounds.

Validate finite, strictly increasing raw and normalized x knots once during
construction, including for splines. Reject duplicates, reversed knots and
non-finite samples. A protected interval-capacity argument lets splines reject
oversized sources before any source reads. Linear y interpolation uses an
oriented weighted blend, so decreasing y values remain supported.

No sample buffer is allocated; the obsolete output-index Range is removed.
Sources must remain stable while an interpolator borrows them.

Validation: new interpolation_bounds regression plus updated endpoint
expectations in existing spline/numeric checks pass with UBSan for float/FP16.
